  <running_head>MATER / ARIUM</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">5. An possit obligari sine tutoris auctori-</l>
    <l n="2">tate?</l>
    <l n="3">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="4">1. Tutor hereditatem adire non potest.</l>
    <l n="5">2. Eam adit pupillus tutore auctore.</l>
    <l n="6">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="7">1. Praesentia, &amp; consensus tutoris de</l>
    <l n="8">praesenti, requiritur.</l>
    <l n="9">2. Ut tamen moderamen sit adhiben-</l>
    <l n="10">dum.</l>
    <l n="11">3. De moribus juris civilis scrupulositas</l>
    <l n="12">hic est sublata.</l>
    <l n="13">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="14">1. Quandoque non potest intervenire tu-</l>
    <l n="15">toris auctoritas.</l>
    <l n="16">2. Nemo potest esse in re suâ auctor.</l>
    <l n="17">3. Ad alienationem bonorum pupillari-</l>
    <l n="18">um opus est decreto.</l>
    <l n="19">4. Quorundam Statutis eo opus est, licet</l>
    <l n="20">parens sit tutor.</l>
    <l n="21" type="heading" level="1" caput="22" para="true">LIBR. I. INSTIT. TIT. 22.</l>
    <l n="22" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Quibus Mod. Tutel. finit.</l>
    <l n="23" type="heading" level="3" para="true">In Init.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">1. Olim alia erat tutela sexus, alia</l>
    <l n="25">aetatis.</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">2. Tutela finitur pubertate.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">3. Nihilominus tenetur tutor puberis</l>
    <l n="28">negotia imperfecta expedire.</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">4. Quomodo veteres de pubertate judica-</l>
    <l n="30">verint?</l>
    <l n="31" para="true">5. Pubertas in jure multiplex.</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">6. Quid jure Hebraorum obtinuerit?</l>
    <l n="33" para="true">7. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="34" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="35" type="heading" level="1" para="true">ARIUM.</l>
    <l n="36" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="37" para="true">Tutela finitur die incerto vel condi-</l>
    <l n="38">tione existente.</l>
    <l n="39" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">1. Morte tutoris solvitur tutela.</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">2. Non si plures sint tutores uno defuncto</l>
    <l n="42">administratio superstiti adcrescit.</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">3. Hares tutoris imperfecta negotia perfi-</l>
    <l n="44">cere tenetur.</l>
    <l n="45" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="46" para="true">Capitis deminutione tutoris finitur tutela,</l>
    <l n="47">non omnis tamen, nec omnis tutela.</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">Ad tempus concessa, illo adveniente,</l>
    <l n="50">finiuntur.</l>
    <l n="51" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="52" para="true">1. Definit esse tutor, qui remotus, qui ex-</l>
    <l n="53">cusatus in perpetuum, numquam fuit</l>
    <l n="54">tutor, ut non definat esse.</l>
    <l n="55" para="true">2. Definit esse tutor, qui patre restituto,</l>
    <l n="56">reversō, interim tutor fuerat.</l>
    <l n="57" type="heading" level="1" caput="23" para="true">LIBR. I. TIT. 23.</l>
    <l n="58" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Curatoribus.</l>
    <l n="59" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="60" para="true">1. CUra definitur.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">2. Differentia inter curam &amp; tute-</l>
    <l n="62">lam proponitur.</l>
    <l n="63" para="true">3. Minor sine curatore potest obligari.</l>
    <l n="64" para="true">4. Moribus curatorum &amp; tutorum non</l>
    <l n="65">sunt distincta nomina.</l>
    <l n="66" para="true">5. Neque minores sine curatorum aucto-</l>
    <l n="67">ritate obligantur.</l>
    <l n="68" para="true">6. Minor quamdiu minor esse censeatur?</l>
    <l n="69" para="true">7. Jure Mosaico masculi censentur majo-</l>
    <l n="70">res anno 25.</l>
    <l n="71" para="true">8. Consuetudo variat.</l>
    <l n="72" para="true">9. Fœmina de moribus sunt in curâ mari-</l>
    <l n="73">torum, aliter extraneum desiderant</l>
    <l n="74">curatorem.</l>
    <l n="75" type="foot" para="true">1. Tutela finitur omni capitis deminutione pupilli.</l>
    <l n="76" type="foot" para="true">2. Non tamen captivitate.</l>
  </main_text>
